<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Trident</h1>
<p>Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>Tridents were polearm weapons based on the agricultural tool, the pitchfork. Employed exclusively for thrusting, the trident provided a broader surface area upon which to skewer an opponent than did a spear. Variations of the trident design existed in almost all cultures where polearms were used in war. The trident was most famous for its use in the Roman gladiatorial arenas. When not in active combat use, the trident made an excellent tool for moving hay.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the trident is a weapon skill of its own, one of the polearms (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): two-handed, it pierces, it leans on strength, with some dexterity, and it is slow, as two-handed weapons are. It is taught by the barbarians from guild level 16 (up to 80%) and the fighters from guild level 16 (up to 80%).
</p><p><br />
